{"title":"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(very_similar_to_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (very similar to Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(point_to_line_distance_formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (point to line distance formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2022bc83f2acc8bb5b00fcb2cf789ba4c95962.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x+5y=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" /> forms a triangle with the coordinate axes. What is the sum of the lengths of the altitudes of this triangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842b6bcbc86314f5b928483dd02e01fd43166997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 20 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\dfrac{360}{17} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\dfrac{107}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\dfrac{43}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\dfrac{281}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"444\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercepts and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-intercepts to find the intersections of the axes and the line. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52f2821f1a68dc474c90d7acb0e279c7fca51c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Our three vertices are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38ec6a35045b7cc0f04c4989a99570bcc29aee43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6ab8e2a6c5f571336217a7e364627012c837cae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />. Two of our altitudes are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and since it is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> right triangle, the hypotenuse is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Since the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so our final altitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f2139f09ead695f382902b70ad234fc01cd12d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30(2)}{13}=\\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"39\" />. The sum of our altitudes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f209edb73789de0c27ce1757519763f7f59799.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60+156+65}{13}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} \\dfrac{281}{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"206\" height=\"48\" />. Note that there is no need to calculate the final answer after we know that the third altitude has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7ac94a5f6297a7d6aadbd7ba04e3a0a732298908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the only choice with a denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zFHtdWEhriQ\">https://youtu.be/zFHtdWEhriQ</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28very_similar_to_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(very_similar_to_Solution_1)\">Solution 2 (very similar to Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (very similar to Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Noticing that the line has coefficients <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can suspect that we have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle on our hands. Because we want the sum of the altitudes, the third altitude that is not an axis must have a denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Since the other altitudes are integers, we choose the option with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as the denominator, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28point_to_line_distance_formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(point_to_line_distance_formula)\">Solution 3 (point to line distance formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (point to line distance formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to the above solutions, we find that the three vertices of the triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cdf0161b1126428c66e60e7379852a89fb09c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25d38afb38cb21e729f74fc5a880d03d5368e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.\nWe already know the length of two of the altitudes (12 and 5 respectively). To find the third altitude we use the formula for a point to a line:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76bacf605702e7339dca5110a3998a4c3a21ba93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{|Ax_0 + By_0 + C|}{\\sqrt{A^2 + B^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"171\" height=\"45\" /> for the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3ea5ae5f5092b7024a8775d282032dc76120c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_0, y_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> and the line in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8b28632cd333905e52e4c716f028986ddc7eb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Ax + By + C = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Using this formula we plug in the known values:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72fb933918f4757249a344704d8c6ad23e526f21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{|12 \\cdot 0 + 5 \\cdot 0 - 60|}{\\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2}}\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73e5556bb2ef3a3fc062a587549accb4c00bb42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{|-60|}{\\sqrt{169}}\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d91e74528bbc50c170c819eed1b6dae6ee57638e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{60}{13}\\]\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>At this point, we are likely already able to guess that the answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d3dbbf344d16f9a7ca95dad85df0475082db474.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{281}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />, because it is the only choice with the denominator being 13. But, we can still confirm this, just in case, by summing up the three heights:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259228074d9f0be40209edef6f721a7b7fc0f68d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12 + 5 + \\frac{60}{13} = \\frac{156}{13} + \\frac{65}{13} + \\frac{60}{13} = \\boxed{\\frac{281}{13}}\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Kellan Zhang (ThePlenGuy)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B\">2015 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017002401\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 334/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8358/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.266      1 -total\n 63.55%    9.702      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 35.24%    5.379      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14040:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017002401 and revision id 288766. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}